# 9. Why Me?

### 1. I Know This Codebase Inside-Out
With 6 PRs across [ARModel](file:///c:/Users/aftab/Desktop/neural-lam/neural_lam/models/ar_model.py#24-771), [metrics.py](file:///c:/Users/aftab/Desktop/neural-lam/neural_lam/metrics.py), [vis.py](file:///c:/Users/aftab/Desktop/neural-lam/neural_lam/vis.py), and the datastore layer, I have hands-on experience with the exact components this project will restructure. I don't need to "ramp up" — I've already been reading the code, finding bugs, and fixing them.

### 2. My Contributions Target the Right Areas
My PRs are not scattered across unrelated features. They specifically address:
- **Metric aggregation** (PRs #303, #388) → the exact pipeline that needs ensemble-aware extensions
- **Visualization** (PR #340) → the exact module that needs ensemble plotting
- **Testing** (PR #440) → the testing infrastructure for regression verification
- **Data handling** (PRs #333, #386) → the datastore integrity for reliable experiments

### 3. I Understand the Scientific Context
This isn't just a code refactoring project — it's a scientific software engineering challenge. I understand:
- Why ensemble forecasts matter for weather prediction
- How CRPS differs from MSE as an evaluation metric
- What a rank histogram tells you about ensemble calibration
- How variational inference enables stochastic weather models

### 4. I Have the Technical Depth
The project requires comfort with:
- **PyTorch Lightning module patterns** — I've worked with train/val/test steps, distributed training, metric logging
- **Graph neural network architectures** — I understand message passing, hierarchical graphs, and how they map to weather prediction grids
- **Variational generative models** — I'm comfortable with ELBO, KL divergence, reparameterization trick, and posterior collapse mitigation

### 5. I Communicate and Collaborate Well
My PR history shows respectful, responsive engagement with maintainers. I respond to code review feedback promptly and iterate until the code meets the project's quality standards.

